abstract: >-
  Replication package for a study of LLM-generated Wazuh rules. An LLM
  conditioned only on an organization profile writes local rules; over a fixed
  set of 1,000 real SSH authentication events, the LLM-augmented configuration
  lowers accuracy by 4.4 percentage points and weighted F1 by 3.1 relative to
  the native ruleset, with the regression concentrated in a single failure
  mode. The package holds the anonymized dataset, the prompts, the generated
  rule sets, the per-run labeled CSVs, and the scripts that recompute and
  verify every number printed in the paper.
